The '''IB-94 blaster pistol''' was a rare model of [[blaster pistol]] with impressive range and firepower for its small size. It was manufactured by [[BlasTech Industries]].

==Description==
Produced by [[BlasTech Industries]],<ref name="MandoV1">[[The Mandalorian: The Manga, Vol. 1|''The Mandalorian: The Manga'', Vol. 1]]</ref> the IB-94 blaster pistol,<ref name="Rubies II" /> or IB-94 blaster for short, was a small model of [[blaster pistol]]<ref name="MandoV1" /> that possessed both an impressive range and firepower.<ref name="DB">{{Databank|mando-s-blaster|Mando's blaster}}</ref> Due to its small size, the power the pistol held was considered surprising.<ref name="MandoV1" />

==History==
[[File:MandoManga-WieldingPistol.png|thumb|left|300px|Din Djarin makes use of an IB-94]]
The IB-94 became a rare weapon.<ref name="DB" /> Nonetheless, during the [[Imperial Era]], [[T'onga]]<ref name="Bounty Hunters 21">[[Bounty Hunters 21|''Bounty Hunters'' 21]]</ref> and the [[cyborg]] [[Beilert Valance]] wielded this model.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 14">[[Bounty Hunters 14|''Bounty Hunters'' 14]]</ref> As a [[bounty hunter]], the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]] carried an [[The Mandalorian's IB-94 blaster pistol|IB-94]] that served as one of his primary weapons.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> The weapon was vital to Djarin and his efforts to survive the rougher parts of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="DB" />

{{Weapon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The IB-94 first appeared in [[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian|Chapter 1]] of the [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 1" /> which aired on [[November 12]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315150248}}</ref> Its design is based off the [[Wikipedia:Bergmann 1896#M1893 and M1894 prototypes|Bergmann 1894 No. 1]] semi-automatic pistol, albeit with some modifications.<ref name="ForgotWeapon">{{YouTube|video=JvGa2c3rEuE|text=The Mandalorian Carries an 1894 Bergmann No.1|channel=channel/UCrfKGpvbEQXcbe68dzXgJuA|name=Forgotten Weapons}}</ref>

